= Loyola University Chicago Stritch School of Medicine - Prompt 04

#section_label("Prompt metadata")
- Title: Disagreeing with Feedback
- Limit: 500 words
- Cycle used in this repo: 2025-2026 from Med School Insiders
- Source: https://medschoolinsiders.com/medical-school-secondary-prompts-database/loyola-university-secondary-essay-prompts/
- Local notes file: prompt-04.local.md

#section_label("Prompt text")
Describe a time you received feedback about your performance and disagreed with the feedback. What did you disagree with? How did you handle it?

#section_label("Shared backbone files")
- typst/shared/challenge.typ
- typst/shared/values.typ

#section_label("challenge backbone")
= Challenge / Adversity Backbone

== Situation
Describe the challenge clearly and briefly.

== Response
- What did you do?
- What tradeoffs or hard decisions did you make?
- Who did you rely on?

== Growth
- What changed in you?
- How will this matter in medicine?
#section_label("values backbone")
= Values / Professionalism Backbone

== Value
Choose one value you can prove with behavior.

== Example
Tell the story that demonstrates the value under pressure.

== Reflection
Explain how that value will show up in medicine.

